~ escapee
Narrator: Behind the wet boxwood hedge, a shivering patient wipes chalky white dust from their palms onto a hospital smock.
mr_escapee [afraid]: Hush, do not call the masks, I crushed the little white pills in my pocket for three days running. My head is coming clear, and there is a cellar smell of wet worms on the draught, I have to get over this hedge...
* Stand aside -> escapee_aside
* Help them over the hedge -> escapee_help
* Stop them -> escapee_stop

~ escapee_aside
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_hatch_found
set mr_hatch_hint
Narrator: Glass shatters overhead as a towering bulk drops from an upper casement into the rain-soaked grass, folding the trembling runner into arms like oak boughs.
hugo [sad]: Oh, little bird, Hugo hears you crying from the window. Come inside out of the wet, Hugo will help, Hugo will carry you down by the quiet room with the floor hatch.
-> END

~ escapee_help
set mr_escapee_helped
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_conduct_strikes += 1
Narrator: You boost the patient over the dripping briars into the mist, just as two white porcelain masks turn toward you from the terrace steps.
mr_escapee [afraid]: Bless you, strangers, do not drink the sweet water if you want to keep your names.
-> END

~ escapee_stop
set mr_escapee_seen
set mr_powdered
damage 1d4 poison
Narrator: As {name} catches the patient's sleeve, they fling their hands up and a cloud of bitter white pill-dust catches in {name}'s throat.
mr_escapee [sad]: No, no, you have made me spill it, and the orderlies are already coming with the cup...
-> END
